  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(8).$ Therefore, $\\lambda =8,$ which means that $8$ customers buy an anniversary card each hour. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{h}=7.5\\,\\text{min}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average time until the next customer buys an anniversary card is $7.5$ minutes.",
